    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leading the offensive charge. With a score of 67.11, he is our most reliable asset against Legumina, benefiting from a favorable 4.32 xERA matchup and a prime spot in the #2 hole. While the dynamic platoon disadvantage against a right-hander pulls his raw projection down slightly, the park factor and high-leverage order placement cement him as the focal point of the daily lineup. **Drake Baldwin** is our next strongest play at 59.15; while facing a respectable 3.98 xERA from Hart, his ascension to the leadoff spot provides a +10% boost to his efficiency score, making him a high-floor target for Runs and OBP-adjacent value today.\n\nThe middle of our lineup is currently grinding through tougher conditions. **Brayan Rocchio** sits at a marginal 44.53, largely due to a difficult matchup against Bradley\u2019s 3.82 xERA, which effectively negates his value despite the stability he offers in the #4 slot. Similarly, **Dominic Smith** is teetering on the edge of our bench threshold at 40.68. A same-handed platoon disadvantage against Hart significantly dampens his outlook, and he remains in the lineup only because of the lack of superior utility alternatives currently available. \n\nOur bench optimization was relatively straightforward today due to several key players, including **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, sitting on an off-day. **Jackson Merrill** was the most notable \"near-miss\" for the starting lineup; however, his sub-optimal 3.14 xERA matchup against Sale, coupled with the inherent risks of a same-handed platoon disadvantage, resulted in an automatic benching in today's projection model. We continue to monitor the status of depth pieces like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Heliot Ramos**, but for this specific 5x5 rotation, we are keeping our exposure limited to the players currently posted. No severe weather flags are present, but managers should keep a close eye on the official lineups for **Drake Baldwin** and **Dominic Smith**, as any late-scratch or order-tinkering could drop their efficiency scores below our 40-point start threshold.",
